		{
			dependencies: ["664F03BCD6779986"]
			description: [
				"   Catalysts are auxiliary components inserted into the process to alter its behavior: they accelerate, divert, amplify. They’re not mandatory — until they are."
				""
				"   In most cases, they’re the only way to extract rare by-products like ilmenite, rutile, obsidianite, or things even less pronounceable. Treat them with care — actually, with planning."
				""
				"   They will decide whether your industrial chain is efficient… or just loud."
				""
				"   Ground quartz acts as a crystalline abrasive inside the pulverizer chamber. Its sharp edges and high hardness index mechanically interfere with ore fragmentation, helping destabilize micro-structures."
				""
				"   Though not participating chemically, its silicate nature improves cutting action, speeding up milling. However, like any light abrasive, it wears easily, being more useful for short, low-demand sessions."
				""
				"&7&o— Cuts well, lasts little. Like many speeches.&r&r"
			]
			id: "377D66DD47488FE4"
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5601627FBBA59813"
				item: "mekanism:dust_quartz"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Abrasive Efficiency"
			x: -3.5d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["377D66DD47488FE4"]
			description: [
				"   Everyone treats the &6Pulverizer&r like a rock blender. It's a slot machine, and catalysts are how you load the dice."
				""
				"   &6Coke Dust&r loads them for speed and leftovers: &a1.5×&r secondary output, never below a &a35%&r chance, &a30%&r of the normal energy per run. It also burns through itself, gone &a60%&r of the time."
				""
				"   So it's not for hoarding rare dusts (that's &6Rich Slag&r, patient and boring). It's for when a line of raw ore is backing up and you want it cleared, with a little extra on the way out."
				""
				"&7&o— Fast, greedy and short-lived. Sounds like most of my ideas.&r&r"
			]
			id: "25FED667BD6B99AD"
			shape: "gear"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6FD3BD75DC351BD3"
				item: "immersiveengineering:dust_coke"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Reactive Combustion"
			x: -5.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
