		}
		{
			dependencies: ["504BB1A0C0A5D778"]
			description: [
				"   This viscous substance, derived from complex biological processes, acts as an active solvation medium inside the chamber. Its gelatinous composition encapsulates particles during milling, preventing suspension losses and optimizing secondary reactions."
				""
				"   In addition, certain unstable organic compounds within it serve as precursors for catalytic reactions, especially with minerals sensitive to pH or organo-metallic bonding. Its durability and yield make it the gold-standard catalyst. Excellent and balanced — it could just last a little longer..."
				""
				"&7&o— It dissolves things you didn’t know were there. Including your certainty.&r&r"
			]
			id: "0E15CFE7649C8E5E"
			shape: "gear"
			tasks: [{
				id: "77215FC08FA0171E"
				item: "kubejs:gelatinous_organic_solvent"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Bio-Structural Catalyst"
			x: -5.0d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"4807891B99079DE0"
				"3321B64AAB3C71A1"
			]
			description: [
				"   Cinnabar, primarily mercury sulfide (HgS), has a crystalline structure that, when stressed, releases micro-static charges and undergoes lamellar fracture."
				""
				"   During pulverization, these effects cause electrostatic dispersion of particulates, reducing agglomeration and increasing surface exposure for processing. Its balanced performance makes it a broadly applicable technical catalyst."
				""
				"&7&o— Beauty lies in balance… and in a slight degree of functional toxicity.&r&r"
			]
			id: "1F6EBFB9DB2A2B14"
			shape: "gear"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6D2A60FB21D90FE1"
				item: "thermal:cinnabar"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Red Crystal Reagent"
			x: -5.0d
			y: -0.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4B17B25AEC9A0007"]
			description: [
				"   Counter-intuitive as it is, the Ice Charge works as a moderating thermal agent. During milling, its controlled cold release absorbs part of the friction-generated energy, reducing system wear and enabling short cycles with fewer interruptions."
				""
				"   Its action is purely physical and limited, but the agility it provides is valuable in fast-processing flows. Fragile and volatile, it rarely survives more than a single round."
				""
				"&7&o— It doesn’t last long, but it cools tempers and speeds the work. A temporary relief — like a good improbable argument.&r&r"
			]
			id: "1DB47027209C4091"
			shape: "gear"
			tasks: [{
				id: "418CDA44CA87730C"
				item: "thermal:ice_charge"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Directed Thermal Shock"
			x: -5.0d
			y: 2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["42B368C1DD78B214"]
			description: [
				"   Formed by blast-furnace residues rich in metal oxides, Rich Slag acts as a promoter of surface reactivity. Its components — chiefly iron, silicon, and aluminum oxides — interact with particles under fracture, increasing their chemical instability."
				"   This effect induces the release of by-products bound by weak forces or requiring minimal catalytic activation. Though it doesn’t affect speed, its efficiency in secondary extractions is exceptional."
				""
				"&7&o— What’s left from smelting… now extracts what never left the stone. Second chances for catalysts and sinners.&r&r"
			]
			id: "41F84F8BA400D58F"
			shape: "gear"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4C1F251E95EB52D8"
				item: "thermal:rich_slag"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Reprocessed Purity Residue"
			x: -5.0d
			y: 4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5697C0E23B256642"]
			description: [
				"   Given too much stimulus, even a plant yields. In the Phytogenic Insolator, under constant light, pure water, and excess Phyto-Gro, it tries to protect itself. It closes its stomata. Reinforces its fibers. Stiffens its cell walls until it becomes… something else. Something dead."
				""
				"   Instead of blooming, it forms a carapace of dense cellulose and modified lignin — a defense reaction that, ironically, suffocates it. Without noticing, the plant literally embalms itself to death, an “auto-immune disease.” The result is Organic Polymer Mesh: a high-performance plant polymer, flexible, heat-resistant, and completely inert. Perfect for machines. Horrible for photosynthesis."
				""
				"   Curious how we chase dense, rare metals only to find the chapter’s most useful material comes from plants and water. Don’t underestimate &2&lgreen engineering!&r&r"
				""
				"&7&o— Fascinating. Give a plant paradise and it embalms itself.&r&r"
			]
			id: "1E7A8B399C39BF92"
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [{
				id: "7B017C8ACAC68D96"
				item: "kubejs:organic_polymer_mesh"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -2.5d
			y: 6.0d
		}
